WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.119 --> 00:00:04.850
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie congrats to everyone
who’s made it to one of the Doctor Who World

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.920
Tour stops. As I’m posting this video they’re
headed to Seoul South Korea. Some of you even

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.799
sent me some selfies you got with them. Which
is totally awesome.

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:19.020
The official Doctor Who team actually made
a special request for a very specific video

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.329
from me. I’ll explain that at the end of
this video because it will be something different.

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:30.239
The biggest news is that Peter Capaldi just
signed on for series 9. Which makes me very

00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:35.010
relieved. I think you can tell an interesting
story in one series. Christopher Eccleston

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.519
only did one, but now Capaldi has two full
years to develop his character.

00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:45.379
This video is mostly going to be about what
Moffat has been saying and not saying about

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:49.050
the current run. But I will mention things
I’d like to see in series 9. The biggest

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:55.920
things aside from Capaldi returning were him
being pretty upfront about a big villain being

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.600
dead and gone and there’s a new spinoff
that he’s trying to slip through the cracks

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.609
in the universe.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.910
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I do weekly Doctor Who videos, I’m

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:10.780
even doing a weekly giveaway all you have
to do to enter is be a subscriber and leave

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:11.990
a comment on this video.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.860
So most important stuff first. If you have
seen the screenings of episode 1 at Cardiff

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.910
or London or you watched the leak, please
use spoiler tags when commenting about it.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.380
There is a brand new title sequence and it
is glorious. It’s way different from Matt

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.270
Smith’s intro.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.900
Peter Capaldi’s Doctor is the end to Matt
Smith’s fairytale era. So anyone who quit

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:36.020
the show because of that will probably enjoy
the new series. Until they find something

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.610
else to complain about.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:42.920
Because he’s coming back in 2015 expect
the same themes to continue from series to

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.330
series. It’s still Moffat running the show
so using Matt Smith’s run for comparison,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.430
the tone of the show didn’t change too much
between series 5 and 7b. It was always a fairy

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:56.400
tale relationship comedy. You just noticed
it more whenever River Song was around.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.390
I know a lot of you guys are asking about
her. She wasn’t the person Moffat was talking

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:09.390
about last week, but previously he’s said
Name of The Doctor was her finale. As fans

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:15.310
we can have some fun and theorycraft, but
for all intents and purposes, do not expect

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:22.310
to see her in series 8. When we do get to
the episodes I’ll mention anything I think

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:28.549
is a potential easter egg for her though.

00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:32.760
Capaldi’s Doctor into Darkness as the trailer
implies is going to have the same tone from

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:39.760
series 8 to 9. Even if a lot of the characters
and plots get shuffled. We kind of have to

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.090
wait to see episodes before we get a solid
idea of how they’re going explain the darkness

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:53.209
in his soul.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:56.629
Spoiler people please remember to use tags
if you’ve read ahead in the scripts.

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:00.430
They actually did release a clip from Episode
2. I didn’t want to flat out post it without

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.549
a spoiler warning so careful if you don’t
want to know anything about episode 2. Just

00:03:04.549 --> 00:03:09.840
skip forward in the video 30 seconds. I’ll
wait just a sec….okay, here we go.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.200
The episode 2 clip is of them messing with
a broken Dalek. I haven’t read the script

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:18.829
but the footage was from a promo cut with
a generic capaldi interview on BBC One. These

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:23.420
promos don’t run in the United States so
if you’re a UK person let us know in the

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:28.620
comments if they normally use footage from
new episodes ahead of time in promos.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:34.069
The trailers are usually less spoilery. But
whatever, into the Dalek is a very literal

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:37.400
way to view Capaldi’s journey into Darkness.
Even though it’s implied in the clip that

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.760
In the past usually when The Doctor has messed
with Dalek innards he’s trying to access

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.180
their data core to get information. Physically
traveling inside a Dalek is a whole other

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.919
thing. It’s like taking a magic school bus
ride to Hell.

00:03:49.919 --> 00:03:55.409
I think one of the biggest complaints against
series 8 so far has been the re-use of old

00:03:55.409 --> 00:03:59.549
characters and villains. For the most part
that’s true, we’ve all seen the Cybermen

00:03:59.549 --> 00:04:04.019
from the finale, the Daleks in the trailer
and the Paternoster Gang. It’s even implied

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:07.739
that the Clockwork droids from Girl in the
Fireplace are back, that was from Russell

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:12.349
T Davies run, but Stephen Moffat wrote the
episode. So he created the clockwork droids.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:15.090
I don’t mind the idea of seeing familiar
characters as long as they’re done in a

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.849
very different way. The only time I think
it takes you out of the episode is when it’s

00:04:18.849 --> 00:04:22.870
something or someone you just saw in the previous
episode. If there were Daleks everywhere in

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.550
the Series 8 premiere I’d be disappointed.
But I don’t mind Daleks in episode 2 given

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.770
that we’ll see it in a way we never have
before.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.479
You guys let me know, is there anything from
Matt Smith’s run that would really make

00:04:33.479 --> 00:04:40.479
you upset if it showed up in series 8?

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.360
Just based on previous comments you’ve made
it seems like the most polarizing is River

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.560
Song. It’s like half the fandom really hated
her and half really loved her. But if there’s

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.310
anything besides her that you feel very strongly
about just write it in the comments.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.520
The longer Doctor Who as a series continues,
the harder it is for them to do something

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.400
completely new. Something that’s never been
done.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.250
From the early reports I’ve been seeing,
people are saying that Capaldi is a very thoughtful

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:07.900
if not welcome analog to the third and fourth
doctors. Which totally makes sense, John Pertwee

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.819
was his childhood Doctor. During that run
he even wrote his own fan fiction scripts

00:05:11.819 --> 00:05:17.060
and sent them to the Doctor Who offices. He
did it so much it impressed Barry Letts, the

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:22.580
producer at that time, who invited Capaldi
to the BBC offices to meet Pertwee and Terrence

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.599
Dicks. Dicks was the script editor during
those years so he would have probably read

00:05:26.599 --> 00:05:33.599
Capaldi’s fan scripts.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:43.900
It would be so amazing if the BBC organized
a cast reading of his scripts with all the

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:48.099
actors roleplaying the parts. They could even
get Sean Pertwee from Musketeers to play his

00:05:48.099 --> 00:05:52.330
father’s role. I think it would be too on
the nose to have Capaldi play the third doctor.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:56.860
I think he would have been somewhere between
age 13 and 16 when he wrote all of them. I

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:01.009
don’t know which year he actually visited
the offices. But to all you teenagers writing

00:06:01.009 --> 00:06:07.659
fan fiction on tumblr keep it up. If it’s
good someone will notice.

00:06:07.659 --> 00:06:14.659
A lot of times actors like Peter Dinklage
on Game of Thrones stay away from the source

00:06:14.849 --> 00:06:18.810
material just so it won’t influence their
take on the character too much, but in Capaldi’s

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:23.139
case I think it totally works. Doctor Who
is meta science fiction, it totally makes

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:28.310
sense that a 2000 plus year old person would
mix and match references and affectations

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.270
from previous lives.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:34.349
Let me know if you agree, will a superfan
of Doctor Who make a better Doctor than someone

00:06:34.349 --> 00:06:36.080
who never watched it before in their life?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:42.879
The other big takeaway from the early Episode
1 talk is the Paternoster Spinoff. It’s

00:06:42.879 --> 00:06:49.539
felt like every time Moffat uses them it’s
a backdoor spinoff but supposedly he’s really

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:55.520
pushing for it in series 8. We’ve all seen
the pictures from episode 1 but I think I

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.270
mentioned in an older video that the characters
are going to be featured at the end of series

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:00.689
8 too.

00:07:00.689 --> 00:07:04.189
I don’t know how they’re involved, only
that I think they appeared on a casting sheet

00:07:04.189 --> 00:07:08.330
for somewhere in the last few episodes. That
would make sense if Moffat is really trying

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.830
to get another spinoff going.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:14.030
Sarah Jane and Torchwood were the last successful
ones. I didn’t watch Sarah Jane but I was

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.889
a huge fan of Torchwood. To anyone hoping
to see Captain Jack again, I think you’re

00:07:17.889 --> 00:07:24.889
going to be dissapointed. John Barrowman has
said that he was never contacted at any time

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:29.979
during Moffat’s run to appear in the specials
or any of the episodes. He said he doesn’t

00:07:29.979 --> 00:07:31.110
ever expect to see Captain Jack on screen
again at all.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:35.169
Just because Captain Jack was Russell T Davies
baby and Moffat wants to do his own thing.

00:07:35.169 --> 00:07:38.669
Even though the Clockwork droids were both
his and Russell T Davies.

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:42.270
That’s just John Barrowman talking himself,
it’s up to Moffat who comes back.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:46.699
Here’s an interesting question though, would
you watch a Paternoster series?

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:51.249
Think about it in terms of the characters,
Doctor Who is a series marketed to children

00:07:51.249 --> 00:07:57.960
and millennials, so you get mature themes
with a lot of humor and morality. Torchwood

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:02.830
was designed for an older more mature audience.
So you get more mature subject matter.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:08.020
The Paternoster characters read like they’re
meant for a younger audience, like a paternoster

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.639
spinoff would be more for children. Just re-watch
any scene with Strax in it. Madam Vastra and

00:08:12.639 --> 00:08:17.300
Jenny could go either way, but I feel like
Strax is there for children.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:22.050
During series 7 the BBC even produced some
bonus strax videos with him visiting children’s

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:22.460
classrooms.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:26.669
I’ll go on record as saying I’ll watch
anything produced under the Doctor Who umbrella.

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:31.139
Good or bad. But Game of Thrones is my jam,
so if we get a Paternoster Spinoff I’d like

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:35.120
to see Vastra disembowel someone with her
teeth on occasion.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:40.500
Either way, the Paternoster Gang are here
to stay Spinoff or no Spinoff. The big character

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:45.389
Moffat said was definitely gone for good was
The Master. I know huge bummer.

00:08:45.389 --> 00:08:51.019
Earlier this year it was reported that the
BBC was testing new actors for The Master,

00:08:51.019 --> 00:08:54.579
right now John Simm is still the Master, an
amazing Master. But he’s busy with his new

00:08:54.579 --> 00:08:57.700
series Intruders. So he wouldn’t be able
to return even if Moffat wanted him. Which

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:58.820
he doesn’t.

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:04.040
His comment was that he felt Russell T Davies
did such a good job with the character, Moffat

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.810
didn’t think he had anything he could add
to it.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.899
Thus we shall have no Master in series 8.

00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:15.279
I don’t know anything about the villain
teased in the first episode or how it plays

00:09:15.279 --> 00:09:16.829
into the finale. But there have been reports
that it seems like someone familiar. I’m

00:09:16.829 --> 00:09:19.450
going to wait to talk more about that till
after Episode 1 premieres.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.899
So if you have seen the first episode let
me know what you think, be sure to use spoiler

00:09:23.899 --> 00:09:27.550
tags if you’re going to get really specific.
I know I haven’t mentioned much about Samuel

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:31.810
Anderson. He’s been traveling with them
on the world tour. He’s not set to debut

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.959
till the third or fourth episode I think.
He seems like he’ll be a lot of fun.

00:09:34.959 --> 00:09:39.889
So real quick congratulations to last week’s
giveaway winner. Congratulations to Wobberston

00:09:39.889 --> 00:09:44.170
and Simply Maya Beautiful. You guys both win
Amazon giftcards. I know I said the giveaway

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:48.720
is only for one but I’m so happy the BBC
is giving me shoutouts that I’m doubling

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.920
it. If I’m super happy I will double or
triple the giveaway randomly just because.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.160
usually I don’t announce that thing. I’ll
just pick a few extra people week to week.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.950
Just to explain the BBC request I got. They
saw my Beginners guide video and thought it

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:05.000
would be fun to do the same thing for Classic
Who. So that’s going to be my next video.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.570
Mostly it’s going to draw from The Third
and Fourth Doctor’s runs, but it will be

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.410
a big list. Be sure to subscribe to get that.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:16.120
If you haven’t seen it, click here for that
Series 8 Beginner’s Guide with a list of

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.180
essential episodes and you can click here
for my top 10 people I’d like to see as

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.029
companions in series 9.

00:10:21.029 --> 00:10:23.559
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High fives!

